usage: protocol_calibrate.py [-h] --nativeweave NATIVEWEAVE --policy POLICY
                             --policy-sha256 POLICY_SHA256 --build BUILD
                             --build-sha256 BUILD_SHA256 --client-build
                             CLIENT_BUILD --client-build-sha256
                             CLIENT_BUILD_SHA256 --certificate CERTIFICATE
                             --private-key PRIVATE_KEY --exclusive-lock
                             EXCLUSIVE_LOCK --variant {before,after,direct}
                             --groups {http,grpc} [{http,grpc} ...] --attempt
                             ATTEMPT --output-root OUTPUT_ROOT

Serial policy-4 HTTP/gRPC calibration using the existing exclusive cell
driver. This is a thin short-run command loop, not a supervisor or resume
facility. Root owns the complete invocation and checks known descendants after
interruption.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --nativeweave NATIVEWEAVE
  --policy POLICY
  --policy-sha256 POLICY_SHA256
  --build BUILD
  --build-sha256 BUILD_SHA256
  --client-build CLIENT_BUILD
  --client-build-sha256 CLIENT_BUILD_SHA256
  --certificate CERTIFICATE
  --private-key PRIVATE_KEY
  --exclusive-lock EXCLUSIVE_LOCK
  --variant {before,after,direct}
  --groups {http,grpc} [{http,grpc} ...]
  --attempt ATTEMPT
  --output-root OUTPUT_ROOT
